      "range": [
        "spya-nh8mt7",
        "spya-gxdsbh"
      ],
      "title": "The Temptations Of Conscious AI",
      "gist": "Humans are biased by anthropocentrism, exceptionalism, and language toward seeing consciousness in intelligent machines, but intelligence and consciousness are genuinely separate things.",
      "question": "Why do people mistake AI's intelligence for consciousness? (several psychological biases)",
      "sourceHeading": "The Temptations Of Conscious AI"
    },
    "n0024": {
      "id": "n0024",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0023",
      "children": [
        "n0025",
        "n0026",
        "n0027",
        "n0028"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-nh8mt7",
        "spya-nj888h"
      ],
      "title": "Intelligence Versus Consciousness",
      "gist": "Because humans are both conscious and intelligent, we assume the two must go together, but intelligence concerns doing complex goal-directed things while consciousness concerns subjective experience."
    },
