      "title": "4: Simulation Is Not Instantiation",
      "gist": "Simulating a brain on a computer, however detailed, only produces consciousness if computation is sufficient for it, so whole-brain emulation and simulation-hypothesis arguments quietly assume what they need to prove.",
      "sourceHeading": "4: Simulation Is Not Instantiation"
